import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Measurements from '../components/Measurements.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Halowin Bubo" description="Halowin Bubo is a fork of gufo, ported to native Windows with AMD HIP. See measured speeds, test conditions, and documentation.">
  <span class="eyebrow">Native Windows · AMD HIP</span>
  <h1>Halowin Bubo</h1>
  <p class="intro">Halowin Bubo is a fork of the open-source gufo LLM server. It runs on native Windows with AMD HIP. It is tuned for AMD Strix Halo laptops at about 70 W.</p>
  <div class="credit intro">Bubo is built on <a href="https://github.com/gufo-org/gufo">gufo</a>. Credit goes to the gufo authors for the upstream server. gufo uses the MIT license.</div>
  <div class="article-grid">
    <div class="article-body">
      <section aria-labelledby="for"><h2 id="for">For your Windows laptop</h2><p><strong>Supported hardware:</strong> Bubo is built and tested for AMD Strix Halo with 128 GB of memory on Windows, mainly laptops. It can work on other machines, but we make no promise.</p><p>Bubo is tuned for Ryzen AI Max laptops with Radeon 8060S graphics. Use Qwen3.8 Flash Next in GGUF format with the UD-Q4_K_XL quant. Use Performance mode at about 70 W.</p><p><a href="/docs/system-setup/">Set up your system</a> before you install Bubo.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="speed">
        <h2 id="speed">Measured speed</h2>
        <p>Halowin Bubo on the ASUS ProArt PX13 with Radeon 8060S. Windows 11, Performance mode, about 70 W. Qwen3.8 Flash Next UD-Q4_K_XL with an MTP draft head. Tests: 8–12 October 2026.</p>
        <Measurements />
        <p class="benchmark-comparison">With several users at once, Halowin Bubo with MTP reaches 37.4 tok/s for 1 user, 79.2 for 4 users and about 100–107 for 8 users (combined decode, 4K context each, about 70 W). It is ahead of upstream gufo’s published 1-user MTP rate and level with it at 4 users. At 8 users it runs at about 70 W against upstream’s full-power hardware. <a href="/docs/benchmarks/#many-users">See the table</a>.</p>
        <p class="benchmark-comparison">Reasoning check against stock gufo on 35 GPQA, AIME, HMMT and IMO requests: 29/35 correct for Halowin Bubo and 27/35 for stock gufo, with about 24 % faster decode. No loss of accuracy; the sets are small. <a href="/docs/benchmarks/">See the table</a>.</p>
        <a href="/docs/benchmarks/">Read the benchmark details</a>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="models"><h2 id="models">Supported models</h2><p>Bubo keeps all model families of gufo: DeepSeek V4 Flash, Qwen3.8 27B, Qwen3.8 Flash-Next, Qwen3.6 35B-A3B, Qwen3-ASR 1.7B, Qwen3-TTS 1.7B, Qwen-Image-2.1, and MiniMax H3.</p><p>Bubo is tuned for Qwen3.8 Flash Next. The other models run with upstream gufo settings.</p><p>The default model is an abliterated build of Qwen3.8 Flash Next (from Huihui). It refuses less than the original. The benchmarks on this site use it, and the twin and the draft head match it. Read the usage warnings on its model card. The plain Qwen shards also run, without the twin and the draft head.</p><p>The default profile trades exact output for speed: it accepts near-miss drafts in thinking text. <code>--profile exact</code> matched the stock reference token for token in our proof.</p><a href="/docs/models/">See the model table</a></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="downloads"><h2 id="downloads">Downloads</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo/releases/tag/v0.1.0">Halowin Bubo v0.1.0 for Windows (zip and SHA-256) on GitHub</a>. Open source, MIT licence. This is the first release: see the <a href="/docs/known-issues/">known issues</a>.</p><p><strong>You need:</strong> Windows 11, an AMD Strix Halo machine with 128 GB of memory (96 GB set as GPU memory and a 128 GB page file), the Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable (x64) and about 113 GiB of free disk for the model files. Other 128 GB machines with the same chip may work. We make no promise.</p></section>
    </div>
    <aside class="margin-note" aria-label="Halowin Bubo notes">
      <h2>Documentation</h2><p><a href="/docs/">Read the Halowin Bubo docs</a> for system settings, profiles, and known issues.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
